{"id":1929,"slug":"bigger-than-life","title":"Bigger Than Life","year":1956,"country":"United States","duration":95,"spine":507,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/1929-bigger-than-life","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/d4d406ae48cd0fbfc78216e2efb5bf43/NEeX7phTkN3xjrd1deXb0RmokIXDG3_large.jpg","description":"Though ignored at the time of its release, Nicholas Ray’s Bigger Than Life is now recognized as one of the great American films of the 1950s. When a friendly, successful suburban teacher and father (James Mason, in one of his most indelible roles) is prescribed cortisone for a painful, possibly fatal affliction, he grows dangerously addicted to the experimental drug, resulting in his transformation into a psychotic and ultimately violent household despot. This Eisenhower-era throat-grabber, shot in expressive CinemaScope, is an excoriating take on the nuclear family. That it came in the day of Father Knows Best makes it all the more shocking—and wildly entertaining.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Nicholas Ray","slug":"nicholas-ray"}],"cast":[{"actor":"James Mason","role":"Ed Avery","slug":"james-mason"},{"actor":"Barbara Rush","role":"Lou Avery","slug":"barbara-rush"},{"actor":"Walter Matthau","role":"Wally Gibbs","slug":"walter-matthau"},{"actor":"Robert Simon","role":"Dr. Norton","slug":"robert-simon"},{"actor":"Christopher Olsen","role":"Richie Avery","slug":"christopher-olsen"},{"actor":"Roland Winters","role":"Dr. Ruric","slug":"roland-winters"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Nicholas Ray","slug":"nicholas-ray"},{"role":"Producer","person":"James Mason","slug":"james-mason"},{"role":"Story and screenplay","person":"Cyril Hume","slug":null},{"role":"Story and screenplay","person":"Richard Maibaum","slug":null},{"role":"Based on an article in the New Yorker by","person":"Burton Roueché","slug":null},{"role":"Cinematography","person":"Joe MacDonald, A.S.C.","slug":null},{"role":"Music","person":"David Rak